      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Percutaneous pulmonary valve implantation has been widely accepted as an alternative to surgery in selected patients with right ventricular outflow tract (RVOT) dysfunction. This totally new field of our specialty pushed centres to rethink overall strategies on how to treat RVOT dysfunction. In this review, we will focus on challenges related to patient selection, and discuss innovative procedural techniques developed over the years to enlarge the number of candidates for the technique."},
